decisions_for_burhan:
Strict tolerance for M8. M8's cells run at 1 ms, where EDT at 1 L is accepted 0 % of the time. Choose one:
- run the EDT cells at 0.2 ms, which also needs noise calibration at 0.2 ms;
- gate EDT at 5 L;
- gate T30 only (item 2 of the 23:17 list).

How the band is shown:
- [lo, hi] or value +- half-width;
- whether a refused band's point value is shown (all_bands returns it on band_too_wide);
- whether upstream's EDT sits beside it as 'I-Simpa compatible', and how it is labelled under the no-claim rule.

How energy not in the histogram is bounded (T_max). Options:
- 0, assuming the run holds everything;
- Tail::Bounded, which makes the guarantee depend on a log-linear model;
- a rule for how long a run must go.
The trans_epsilon default belongs to the same decision: SPPS kills particles at -50 dB by default; the preset uses ε 7.
